From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 23:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP: extend SA Query cleanup to legacy MLD reconnects

The upstream SA Query timeout cleanup handles a station that still has an
MLD profile. A former MLD station may instead reconnect as a legacy STA on
an affiliated AP; its MLD profile has already been cleared by authentication,
but the earlier partner link entries still need to be removed. Cover this
case on an AP MLD while preserving the upstream reset of an associated
non-AP MLD. Retain the full-client-state and Open/SAE restrictions so FT
and FILS keys remain intact. A legacy station is reset only after an MFP
SA Query timeout.

Retain the OpenWrt association rollback flow: validate with a new WPA
state machine, restore the old one on failure, and remove old link state
only after successful validation. The reset helper uses check_authorized=0
because the timed-out query permits replacing the earlier association.
Clear the timeout only after a successful reset.

Patch-dependency: 990-02-AP-fix-legacy-station-roaming-between-MLD-links.patch

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -7825,8 +7825,8 @@
 	 * and FILS keep keys of the authentication in the state machine, so
 	 * only Open System and SAE authentication are covered.
 	 */
-	if (hapd->conf->wpa && ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta) &&
-	    ((sta->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC) ||
+	if (hapd->conf->wpa && hapd->conf->mld_ap &&
+	    ((ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta) && (sta->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC)) ||
 	     ((sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MFP) && sta->sa_query_timed_out)) &&
 	    FULL_AP_CLIENT_STATE_SUPP(hapd->iface->drv_flags) &&
 	    (sta->auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_OPEN ||
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -433,6 +433,7 @@
 	if (res < 0)
 		return -1;
 	sta->flags |= WLAN_STA_AUTH;
+	ap_sta_set_sa_query_timeout(hapd, sta, 0);
 	return 0;
 }
 
